   </table><p style="margin-left:3.333%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:2.7pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;margin-right:3.907%;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Thanks, Gary. I'd say on the AI side, is there a way to kind of parse out the demand or new demand that you're seeing relative to maybe the content expansion? And the reason I ask, I'm just trying to understand. Are you driving in &#x2013; I guess it's probably driving both, but what is the bigger one? Is it just increased demand all around or are you just able to sell more products into each one of these solutions?</font></p><p style="margin-left:3.653%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0.7pt;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#a6a6a6;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:8pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">.....................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................</font></p>
